                [
                    127.0,
                    591.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "Summing Up",
            "block_bbox": [
                91,
                656,
                265,
                690
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 6,
            "global_block_id": 6,
            "global_group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    91.0,
                    656.0
                ],
                [
                    265.0,
                    656.0
                ],
                [
                    265.0,
                    690.0
                ],
                [
                    91.0,
                    690.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Writers and readers have reciprocal obligations: in general, writers should write as clearly as possible without distorting or over-simplifying their meaning, and readers should make a good-faith effort to understand difficult writing, because its ideas may be too complex for simple sentences. This relationship is a matter of trust, which makes it a matter of ethics.",
            "block_bbox": [
                90,
                701,
                784,
                828
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 7,
            "global_block_id": 7,
            "global_group_id": 7,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    90.0,
                    701.0
                ],
                [
                    784.0,
                    701.0
                ],
                [
                    784.0,
                    828.0
                ],
                [
                    90.0,
                    828.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "However, not everything is written as clearly as it could be. Sometimes writers have done their best and fallen short, but sometimes they are intentionally unclear. Here are two ethical principles you can follow as a writer or apply as a reader when judging the writing of others:",
            "block_bbox": [
                90,
                832,
                784,
                935
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 7,
            "group_id": 8,
            "global_block_id": 8,
            "global_group_id": 8,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    90.0,
                    832.0
                ],
                [
                    784.0,
                    832.0
                ],
                [
                    784.0,
                    935.0
                ],
                [
                    90.0,
                    935.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The Golden Rule of Style: Write to others as you would have others write to you.",
            "block_bbox": [
                91,
                947,
                764,
                971
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
            "block_order": 8,
            "group_id": 9,
            "global_block_id": 9,
            "global_group_id": 9,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    91.0,
                    947.0
                ],
                [
                    764.0,
                    947.0
                ],
                [
                    764.0,
                    971.0
                ],
                [
                    91.0,
                    971.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "This rule is based on empathy: it asks writers to put themselves in the position of their readers and to evaluate their writing from that perspective. It is an ideal to which ethical writers aspire.",
            "block_bbox": [
                91,
                985,
                785,
                1062
            ],
            "block_id": 10,
            "block_order": 9,
            "group_id": 10,
            "global_block_id": 10,
            "global_group_id": 10,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    91.0,
                    985.0
                ],
                [
                    785.0,
                    985.0
                ],
                [
                    785.0,
                    1062.0
                ],
                [
                    91.0,
                    1062.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The Silver Rule of Style: Do not write to others as you would not have others write to you.",
            "block_bbox": [
                92,
                1075,
                783,
                1125
            ],
            "block_id": 11,
            "block_order": 10,
            "group_id": 11,
            "global_block_id": 11,
            "global_group_id": 11,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    92.0,
                    1075.0
                ],
                [
                    783.0,
                    1075.0
                ],
                [
                    783.0,
                    1125.0
                ],
                [
                    92.0,
                    1125.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "This rule is based on fairness: it acknowledges that the interests of writers and readers may not always align, but it requires that writers not treat readers unfairly, callously, or deceptively. Ethical writers can be expected to follow at least this rule.",
            "block_bbox": [
                90,
                1139,
                784,
                1216
